  "raw_response": {
    "source_context_translations": [
      {
        "context_id": "source-context-9d763a9d06321236e5f1",
        "translation": "Nameless, it is the beginning of Heaven and Earth; named, it is the mother of the myriad things."
      },
      {
        "context_id": "source-context-a0437bbc6bfb969f44fb",
        "translation": "Therefore, always without desire, one may observe its subtlety,"
      },
      {
        "context_id": "source-context-a424d6ece55a7d545520",
        "translation": "and always with desire, one may observe its outward manifestation;"
      },
      {
        "context_id": "source-context-9a8214630e984de604cc",
        "translation": "These two arise together but differ in name; together they are called the mysterious."
      },
      {
        "context_id": "source-context-4413afde456bbd1ce9d9",
        "translation": "When all under Heaven know beauty as beauty, ugliness is already there."
      },
      {
        "context_id": "source-context-4685de02ef89dae1c9bb",
        "translation": "He carries out teaching without words; the myriad things arise and he does not refuse them, gives birth to them but does not possess them, acts but does not rely on them,"
      },
      {
        "context_id": "source-context-feaa73fa76a650622433",
        "translation": "and when merit is accomplished, he does not claim it."
      },
      {
        "context_id": "source-context-360597c69e6676e3f2ab",
        "translation": "It is precisely because he does not claim it that it does not depart."
      },
      {
        "context_id": "source-context-83dbd600117b4d66dde7",
        "translation": "If one does not exalt the worthy, the people will not contend; if one does not prize rare goods, the people will not become thieves; if one does not display what can be desired, the people's hearts and minds will not be disturbed."
      },
      {
        "context_id": "source-context-dfdad13807d31b6c73c3",
        "translation": "so that wise or clever people will not dare to act."
      },
      {
        "context_id": "source-context-b1207290fecf85d73c75",
        "translation": "The Way is empty, yet use of it does not exhaust it; deep and unfathomable, it seems to be the ancestor of the myriad things. It blunts its sharpness, unties its tangle, softens its radiance, and mingles with its dust; deep and still, it seems to exist."
      }
    ],
